{"step_index":1357,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T00:07:24Z","thinking":"**Constructing Zig Benchmark**\n\nI'm now building the NOP-padded equal instruction count benchmark in Zig, focusing on `ops/runtime/equal_instruction_stlf_proof.zig`. It's all about benchmarking two loops: interleaved versus non-interleaved. I'll need to define the design for each loop and ensure equal instruction counts via NOP-padding.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"// ops/runtime/equal_instruction_stlf_proof.zig\\n// NOP-Padded Equal Instruction Count Benchmark & N=30 Statistical Analysis for M4\\n// Guarantees identical instruction counts (8 instrs/iter) between Interleaved and Decoupled loops.\\n\\nconst std = @import(\\\"std\\\");\\nconst print = std.debug.print;\\nconst crdt = @import(\\\"sovra_crdt_kernel.zig\\\");\\n\\nconst c = @cImport({\\n    @cInclude(\\\"time.h\\\");\\n});\\n\\nfn getNanos() u64 {\\n    var ts: c.struct_timespec = undefined;\\n    _ = c.clock_gettime(c.CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &ts);\\n    return @as(u64, @intCast(ts.tv_sec)) * 1_000_000_000 + @as(u64, @intCast(ts.tv_nsec));\\n}\\n\\nfn volatileWrite(ptr: *volatile u64, val: u64) void {\\n    ptr.* = val;\\n}\\n\\nfn nextRandom(state: *u64) u64 {\\n    state.* = state.* *% 6364136223846793005 +% 1442695040888963407;\\n    return state.*;\\n}\\n\\n// Inline NOP helper to pad instructions\\ninline fn padNop3() void {\\n    asm volatile (\\\"nop\\\");\\n    asm volatile (\\\"nop\\\");\\n    asm volatile (\\\"nop\\\");\\n}\\n\\npub fn main() !void {\\n    print(\\\"==========================================================\\\\n\\\", .{});\\n    print(\\\" EQUAL INSTRUCTION COUNT (8 INSTRS) N=30 BENCHMARK (M4)\\\\n\\\", .{});\\n    print(\\\"==========================================================\\\\n\\\\n\\\", .{});\\n\\n    var graph = crdt.SovraCrdtGraph.init();\\n    var rng_seed: u64 = 0x123456789ABCDEF0;\\n\\n    // Warmup Pass\\n    var w: u64 = 0;\\n    while (w < 10000) : (w += 1) {\\n        _ = graph.insert_node(w + 1, .Episode, @as(u8, @intCast(w % 255)), 0);\\n    }\\n    graph.node_count = 0;\\n\\n    const N_RUNS = 30;\\n    var interleaved_times: [N_RUNS]f64 = undefined;\\n    var decoupled_times: [N_RUNS]f64 = undefined;\\n\\n    var volatile_checksum: u64 = 0;\\n    const volatile_ptr: *volatile u64 = &volatile_checksum;\\n\\n    var r: usize = 0;\\n    while (r < N_RUNS) : (r += 1) {\\n        // ---------------------------------------------------------------------\\n        // LOOP A: INTERLEAVED LOOP (8 Instructions: str + immediate ldr STLF)\\n        // --------------------------------\n<truncated 4302 bytes>","Description":"\"Creating NOP-padded equal instruction count STLF proof in Zig\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/ops/runtime/equal_instruction_stlf_proof.zig\"","toolAction":"\"Writing equal_instruction_stlf_proof.zig\"","toolSummary":"\"Writing equal_instruction_stlf_proof.zig\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
