{"step_index":1371,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T00:08:09Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nWith matched instruction counts, the delta isolates to the dependency pattern alone. No reviewer can claim instruction mix contamination anymore. One thing to watch on the n=30 expansion: your variance is already tight at 2%, so the confidence intervals will barely move. The value isn't narrower error bars, it's that 30 samples let you run a proper Shapiro-Wilk normality test before applying the t-distribution. If the distribution is non-normal at n=30, you switch to a bootstrap or Mann-Whitney and you document that switch. Reviewers respect the pivot more than they respect a forced parametric assumption. The wall-clock honesty declaration is the quietest white paper \n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-28T20:08:09-04:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
