{"step_index":1391,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T00:09:09Z","thinking":"**Filtering Output Details**\n\nI'm focused on filtering the output to isolate the JSON object. I've realized that the standard error lines, specifically those indicating execution progress with \"Executing N=30...\", are preceding the JSON. My current strategy involves using Python to parse and filter these lines, looking for the `{\"checksum\"...` indicator to pinpoint the relevant data. I'm planning to update `ops/runtime/shapiro_bootstrap_stlf_audit.py` with this filtering logic.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nSHAPIRO-WILK NORMALITY TEST & NON-PARAMETRIC BOOTSTRAP / MANN-WHITNEY U AUDIT\\nPerforms formal normality testing on N=30 STLF timing data and pivots to non-parametric bootstrap resampling if non-normal.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nimport subprocess\\nimport sys\\nimport numpy as np\\nfrom scipy import stats\\n\\ndef run_statistical_audit():\\n    cmd = \\\"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/ops/runtime/equal_instruction_stlf_proof\\\"\\n    if not os.path.exists(cmd):\\n        print(f\\\"[ERROR] Benchmark binary missing: {cmd}\\\")\\n        return\\n\\n    print(\\\"[*] Executing N=30 Benchmark Binary & Collecting Raw JSON Telemetry...\\\")\\n    raw_bytes = subprocess.check_output([cmd]).decode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    json_line = \\\"\\\"\\n    for line in raw_bytes.splitlines():\\n        line_s = line.strip()\\n        if line_s.startswith(\\\"{\\\") and line_s.endswith(\\\"}\\\"):\\n            json_line = line_s\\n            break\\n\\n    if not json_line:\\n        print(\\\"[ERROR] Failed to locate JSON output line in benchmark output.\\\")\\n        return\\n\\n    data = json.loads(json_line)\\n\\n    arr_a = np.array(data[\\\"interleaved\\\"])\\n    arr_b = np.array(data[\\\"decoupled\\\"])\\n\\n    # 1. Shapiro-Wilk Normality Test\\n    shapiro_a_stat, shapiro_a_p = stats.shapiro(arr_a)\\n    shapiro_b_stat, shapiro_b_p = stats.shapiro(arr_b)\\n\\n    is_a_normal = shapiro_a_p >= 0.05\\n    is_b_normal = shapiro_b_p >= 0.05\\n\\n    print(f\\\"\\\\n[SHAPIRO-WILK NORMALITY TEST (N=30)]\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  • Interleaved Loop : W = {shapiro_a_stat:.4f}, p-value = {shapiro_a_p:.4e} -> ({'NORMAL' if is_a_normal else 'NON-NORMAL (p < 0.05)'})\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  • Decoupled Loop   : W = {shapiro_b_stat:.4f}, p-value = {shapiro_b_p:.4e} -> ({'NORMAL' if is_b_normal else 'NON-NORMAL (p < 0.05)'})\\\")\\n\\n    pivot_needed = not (is_a_normal and is_b_normal)\\n    if pivot_needed:\\n        print(\\\"\\\\n[STATISTICAL PIVOT DECLARED]\\\")\\n        print(\\\"  • Non-normality detected in sample distribution!\\\")\\n        print(\\\"  \n<truncated 2962 bytes>","Description":"\"Updating Shapiro-Wilk audit script for robust JSON line parsing\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/ops/runtime/shapiro_bootstrap_stlf_audit.py\"","toolAction":"\"Updating shapiro_bootstrap_stlf_audit.py JSON line parsing\"","toolSummary":"\"Updating shapiro_bootstrap_stlf_audit.py JSON line parsing\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
